<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ashikaga Yoshinori</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1394–1441</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ashikaga Yoshinori was the sixth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogun</a> of the Ashikaga shogunate, ruling from 1429 to 1441. Chosen by lot from among the sons of Yoshimitsu, he governed autocratically, crushed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamakura">Kamakura</a> kubo <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashikaga-mochiuji">Ashikaga Mochiuji</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eikyo-rebellion">Eikyo Rebellion</a> and punished opponents harshly. He was assassinated in 1441 by the warlord Akamatsu Mitsusuke.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ashikaga-yoshinori.jpg" alt="Ashikaga Yoshinori" width="320" height="341" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 不詳 / Unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ashikaga_Yoshinori_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
